From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:23:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ios: touch controls size (DM_TOUCH_SIZE) on a tested geometry

The virtual gamepad's placement moves out of DmGamepad.m into
DmPadGeometry.h: pure functions of the view's bounds, its safe area, the
DmLayout split and the player's options. Drawing, the hit-test and the
grab read the same values, as before. The built-in size is unchanged.

DM_TOUCH_SIZE=small|medium|large scales every control (0.8, 1, 1.2). A
size that does not fit the screen moves toward medium in steps: every
drawn control stays inside the safe area (the bottom corners reach
halfway into the side insets, as always) and no two overlap.

dm/ios/tests/test_pad_geometry.py builds the header on the Mac with a
small UIKit stand-in and checks iPhone and iPad in landscape, iPad and
split windows in portrait, and iPhone Duo's inner display in portrait,
landscape and tabletop, in 2D and 3D and every size. It also pins the
built-in layout on iPhone Pro Max to the points it has always used.

Upstream-Status: pending (builds on seedds/nxnative#683, which landed as e2fadf22)
Reason: Players ask for smaller or larger touch controls (#347), and the placement needs tests without a device
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#347
